{"id": "medicaid-far-above-the-norm", "title": "13 private provider numbers paid far above the national norm by Medicaid for a service", "seconds": 130.5, "voice": "elevenlabs:exurTFaGNF2gnRcPNH8I", "narrator": "Phil", "tempo": 1.092, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "620e9a15bf4841e6", "words": 414, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Medicaid pays for care for people with low incomes.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 2.66, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Medicaid payments, 2018 to 2024", "sub": "published for the first time in 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.46, 0.72, 0.87, 1.1, 1.24, 1.48, 1.63, 1.8]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "In 2026, the federal government first published what it paid every provider.", "t0": 2.78, "t1": 6.87, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Medicaid payments, 2018 to 2024", "sub": "published for the first time in 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.49, 1.05, 1.18, 1.5, 1.89, 2.19, 2.55, 2.72, 2.84, 3.17, 3.44]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Is a San Francisco provider paid like everyone else?", "t0": 6.99, "t1": 9.9, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Medicaid payments, 2018 to 2024", "sub": "published for the first time in 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.23, 0.42, 0.86, 1.29, 1.51, 1.67, 1.98]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "amount"], "text": "13 private provider numbers here were paid more than 99 in 100 billers nationwide.", "t0": 9.9, "t1": 14.38, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "13 private provider numbers", "sub": "top 1% nationwide, three times the median"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.52, 0.85, 1.22, 1.49, 1.67, 1.81, 2.02, 2.14, 2.3, 2.86, 3.0, 3.15, 3.45, 3.82]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "amount"], "text": "They got three times the usual price per claim, or more. How much in all?", "t0": 14.5, "t1": 18.39, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "13 private provider numbers", "sub": "top 1% nationwide, three times the median"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.37, 0.61, 0.93, 1.06, 1.33, 1.62, 1.77, 2.39, 2.58, 3.29, 3.45, 3.63, 3.73]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "amount"], "text": "32 million dollars.", "t0": 18.39, "t1": 19.84, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$32.0 million", "label": "to 13 private San Francisco provider numbers"}, "emph": ["32"], "wt": [0.04, 0.52, 0.81]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat", "story[5]"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding. An outlier is a reason to look, not proof of anything.", "t0": 20.36, "t1": 24.97, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.34, 0.42, 0.82, 1.04, 1.13, 2.09, 2.28, 2.81, 2.92, 2.99, 3.25, 3.36, 3.66, 3.87, 4.13, 4.24]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "The first lead is price.", "t0": 25.19, "t1": 26.44, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["national median per claim", "1 times"], "b": ["these billers", "3 times or more"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.34, 0.53, 0.64]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "Top 1 percent for a service, and three times the usual price per claim, at once. That’s rare.", "t0": 26.56, "t1": 31.62, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["national median per claim", "1 times"], "b": ["these billers", "3 times or more"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.49, 0.84, 0.99, 1.08, 1.81, 1.99, 2.26, 2.55, 2.68, 2.96, 3.22, 3.36, 3.68, 3.87, 4.46, 4.74]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "13 numbers, 11 operators.", "t0": 31.74, "t1": 33.63, "shot": "b4d", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$16.7 million", "label": "two dialysis clinics of one national company, of $32.0 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.4, 0.95, 1.29]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "Two dialysis clinics of one national company took 16.7 million dollars.", "t0": 33.75, "t1": 38.06, "shot": "b4d", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$16.7 million", "label": "two dialysis clinics of one national company, of $32.0 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.77, 1.08, 1.21, 1.37, 1.71, 2.06, 2.29, 2.82, 3.09, 3.36, 3.65]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "Why might it be fine? One claim can cover many units, and some specialists cost more;", "t0": 38.18, "t1": 44.04, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Units per claim and specialty explain many such rows"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.36, 0.45, 0.59, 1.82, 2.06, 2.34, 2.49, 2.76, 3.01, 3.66, 3.85, 4.06, 4.59, 4.88]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "the claim records would settle each.", "t0": 44.04, "t1": 45.74, "shot": "b5x", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Units per claim and specialty explain many such rows"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.18, 0.44, 0.78, 0.95, 1.25]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[4]"], "text": "A drug check adds nothing: the national drug file flags none of the 13 again, and 10 have no drug money at all.", "t0": 45.86, "t1": 52.16, "shot": "b5w", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Flagged again in the drug file: none of the 13", "No drug money at all: 10 of the 13"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.34, 0.61, 0.88, 1.92, 2.06, 2.41, 2.61, 2.89, 3.28, 3.47, 3.57, 3.67, 4.06, 4.76, 4.96, 5.25, 5.42, 5.57, 5.8, 5.99, 6.09]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "The second lead is speed.", "t0": 52.38, "t1": 53.56, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "New provider numbers", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "$500,000 or more within a year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.45, 0.63, 0.73]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "5 brand-new provider numbers took 500,000 dollars or more within about a year.", "t0": 53.68, "t1": 57.82, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "New provider numbers", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "$500,000 or more within a year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 0.81, 1.17, 1.47, 1.71, 1.92, 2.14, 2.42, 2.68, 2.81, 3.02, 3.26, 3.49, 3.57]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "That’s the classic shape of a billing mill, a fake clinic built to bill fast.", "t0": 57.94, "t1": 61.96, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the classic shape of a billing mill"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.37, 0.77, 1.05, 1.14, 1.21, 1.48, 1.92, 2.07, 2.31, 2.66, 2.93, 3.06, 3.28]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Or of an old practice re-formed as a new company.", "t0": 62.08, "t1": 64.55, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the classic shape of a billing mill"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.27, 0.39, 0.61, 1.07, 1.51, 1.61, 1.69, 1.84]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The third lead: 32 groups the City pays also bill Medicaid themselves.", "t0": 64.77, "t1": 68.91, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The City", "sub": "pays a grant"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "The organization", "sub": "provides care"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Medicaid", "sub": "pays for care too"}], "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.39, 1.17, 1.64, 1.9, 2.02, 2.29, 2.65, 2.97, 3.18, 3.54]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[4]", "notEstablished[8]"], "text": "23 of the 32 are confirmed by an address or an officer; 9 match by name alone.", "t0": 69.03, "t1": 73.61, "shot": "b9n", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["confirmed by a second record", "23"], "b": ["matched by name alone", "9"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.5, 0.58, 0.68, 1.09, 1.22, 1.64, 1.77, 1.84, 2.18, 2.29, 2.4, 3.34, 3.66, 3.92, 4.05, 4.25]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "For 7, Medicaid money is new or tripled since 2021.", "t0": 73.73, "t1": 77.42, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The City", "sub": "pays a grant"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "The organization", "sub": "provides care"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Medicaid", "sub": "pays for care too"}], "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.95, 1.4, 1.68, 1.87, 2.11, 2.24, 2.66, 2.89, 3.19]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "How much in 2024?", "t0": 77.54, "t1": 78.89, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The City", "sub": "pays a grant"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "The organization", "sub": "provides care"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Medicaid", "sub": "pays for care too"}], "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.37, 0.47, 0.71]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "21.4 million dollars.", "t0": 78.89, "t1": 80.64, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$21.4 million", "label": "from Medicaid to 7 City-funded groups, 2024"}, "emph": ["21.4"], "wt": [0.04, 0.51, 0.74, 0.96, 1.26]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "City pay to the same 7 rose too, from 30 million dollars to 46.7 million.", "t0": 81.16, "t1": 86.35, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City pay, fiscal 2022", "$30.0 million"], "b": ["City pay, fiscal 2026", "$46.7 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.54, 0.65, 0.75, 1.08, 1.4, 1.74, 2.47, 2.7, 2.96, 3.21, 3.52, 3.65, 4.13, 4.37, 4.66]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Did one cost get billed to both? Nothing shows that.", "t0": 86.47, "t1": 89.16, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City pay, fiscal 2022", "$30.0 million"], "b": ["City pay, fiscal 2026", "$46.7 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.4, 0.64, 0.8, 1.05, 1.17, 1.82, 2.12, 2.38]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "The fourth lead: in 2023, local billers got 2,174 dollars per enrolled resident.", "t0": 89.38, "t1": 95.53, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["California, 2023", "$1,482"], "b": ["San Francisco, 2023", "$2,174"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.43, 1.25, 1.4, 1.67, 2.24, 2.49, 2.77, 2.97, 3.21, 3.65, 3.82, 4.07, 4.57, 4.94, 5.1, 5.49]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "California: 1,482. 1.47 times as much.", "t0": 95.65, "t1": 100.24, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["California, 2023", "$1,482"], "b": ["San Francisco, 2023", "$2,174"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.9, 1.06, 1.38, 1.56, 1.81, 2.92, 3.11, 3.36, 3.57, 3.83, 4.11, 4.22]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Why so high? A big university hospital and national labs are registered here.", "t0": 100.36, "t1": 104.4, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "City government’s own billers", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "51% of the San Francisco total"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.44, 1.26, 1.4, 1.59, 2.07, 2.49, 2.64, 3.0, 3.28, 3.4, 3.82]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "And City government itself took 51 percent.", "t0": 104.52, "t1": 106.73, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "City government’s own billers", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "51% of the San Francisco total"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.4, 0.7, 1.07, 1.3, 1.75]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[5]"], "text": "At Potrero Avenue, over half of new dialysis patients started with Medi-Cal as their only coverage.", "t0": 106.95, "t1": 111.97, "shot": "record-5-53.8% in 2024", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s2", "text": "53.8% in 2024", "mark": "53.8% in 2024", "kicker": "CMS National Plan and Provider Enumeration System"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.64, 1.23, 1.49, 1.74, 1.83, 1.97, 2.46, 2.82, 3.14, 3.3, 3.86, 4.0, 4.19, 4.48]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "Nothing shows any provider overbilled, and no patient data was used.", "t0": 112.19, "t1": 115.61, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any provider overbilled", "Where patients were treated", "Whether any was disciplined: the State licence files carry no discipline field"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.57, 0.78, 1.24, 1.94, 2.1, 2.26, 2.62, 2.86, 3.02]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[3]"], "text": "Or whether any was disciplined: the State licence files carry no discipline field.", "t0": 115.73, "t1": 119.95, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any provider overbilled", "Where patients were treated", "Whether any was disciplined: the State licence files carry no discipline field"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.4, 0.6, 0.75, 1.76, 1.91, 2.22, 2.62, 3.03, 3.33, 3.46, 3.88]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? Units per claim from the State.", "t0": 120.07, "t1": 122.54, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Units per claim, from the State"}, {"who": "", "what": "City grant budgets beside Medicaid billing"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.3, 0.61, 1.04, 1.38, 1.54, 1.83, 1.99, 2.09]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "And City grant budgets, beside Medicaid bil